# Flutter Donations + Paystack Flow — Cursor Prompt

Copy everything below the line into Cursor inside the Flutter project. The backend API is already live and locked.

> Replace **Riverpod**, **GoRouter**, and **webview_flutter** with whatever the project already uses before pasting.

---

Implement a complete **Donations + Paystack flow** in this Flutter app, integrated with the existing Node.js backend.

## Stack to use

- Flutter (latest stable, null-safe Dart)
- State management: **Riverpod** (match what the project already uses; do not introduce a new state lib)
- HTTP: existing **Dio** client with the auth interceptor (do not create a new one)
- WebView: **webview_flutter** ^4.x
- Routing: existing router (GoRouter or Navigator) — do not switch
- Date / currency: `intl`

## Backend contract (locked, do not change)

Base URL: `https://satya-server-app-2.onrender.com/api/v1`
All endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>`.

Set this once for the curls below:

```bash
BASE_URL="https://satya-server-app-2.onrender.com/api/v1"
TOKEN="YOUR_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN"
```

### 1) List approved + visible donations

```
GET /donations
```

```bash
curl -X GET "$BASE_URL/donations?page=1&limit=10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Response item shape: `{ _id, title, description, image, status, isVisible }`.

### 2) Start a Paystack donation

```
POST /donations/:id/donate
```

Body:
```json
{
  "amount": 100,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "note": "Om Namah",
  "callbackUrl": "https://app.satya.example/donation/return"
}
```
- `amount` required, number, min 10.
- `currency` optional, defaults to `ZAR`.
- `note` optional, max 280 chars.
- `callbackUrl` optional — server falls back to `PAYSTACK_CALLBACK_URL`.

```bash
# Minimal
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/donations/68a1b2c3d4e5f60011223344/donate" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"amount": 100}'

# Full body
curl -X POST "$BASE_URL/donations/68a1b2c3d4e5f60011223344/donate" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "amount": 250,
    "currency": "ZAR",
    "note": "Om Namah Shivaya",
    "callbackUrl": "https://app.satya.example/donation/return"
  }'
```

Response 201 `data`:
```json
{
  "paymentId": "...",
  "contributionId": "...",
  "contributionNumber": "SATYA-DON-10001",
  "reference": "PSK-DON-10001-A1B2C3",
  "authorization_url": "https://checkout.paystack.com/abcd1234",
  "authorizationUrl":   "https://checkout.paystack.com/abcd1234",
  "callbackUrl": "https://satya-server-app-2.onrender.com/payment-success",
  "accessCode": "abcd1234efgh5678",
  "publicKey": "pk_test_...",
  "amount": 250,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "donation": { "_id": "...", "title": "Temple Renovation" }
}
```

The Flutter app should open `authorization_url` in a WebView and intercept navigation to the host of `callbackUrl`.

### 3) Server-side verify (the only source of truth)

```
GET /payments/verify/:reference
```

Idempotent — safe to retry.

```bash
curl -X GET "$BASE_URL/payments/verify/PSK-DON-10001-A1B2C3" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Response `data`:
```json
{
  "status": "success",
  "alreadyPaid": false,
  "payment": { "_id": "...", "status": "SUCCESS", "paymentFor": "DONATION" },
  "contribution": {
    "_id": "...",
    "contributionNumber": "SATYA-DON-10001",
    "amount": 250,
    "currency": "ZAR",
    "paymentStatus": "PAID"
  }
}
```

`status` ∈ `"success" | "failed" | "abandoned" | "unknown"`. Only `"success"` counts as paid.

### 4) My donation history

```
GET /donations/contributions/my
```

```bash
# Default
curl -X GET "$BASE_URL/donations/contributions/my?page=1&limit=10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"

# Filter to PAID
curl -X GET "$BASE_URL/donations/contributions/my?paymentStatus=PAID&limit=20" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"

# Filter by a specific donation
curl -X GET "$BASE_URL/donations/contributions/my?donation=68a1b2c3d4e5f60011223344" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Response `data`:
```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "_id": "...",
      "contributionNumber": "SATYA-DON-10001",
      "amount": 250,
      "currency": "ZAR",
      "paymentStatus": "PAID",
      "paymentMethod": "PAYSTACK",
      "paystackReference": "PSK-DON-10001-A1B2C3",
      "transactionId": "1234567890",
      "note": "Om Namah Shivaya",
      "donation": { "_id": "...", "title": "Temple Renovation", "image": "...", "status": "APPROVED", "isVisible": true },
      "user":     { "_id": "...", "fullName": "Venkat T", "email": "user@example.com" },
      "createdAt": "2026-05-12T13:55:23.014Z"
    }
  ],
  "pagination": { "page": 1, "limit": 10, "total": 1, "totalPages": 1 }
}
```

## End-to-end test sequence

```bash
# 1. Pick a donation
curl -s "$BASE_URL/donations?limit=1" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
DONATION_ID="<paste _id from above>"

# 2. Start a donation
INIT=$(curl -s -X POST "$BASE_URL/donations/$DONATION_ID/donate" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"amount": 50, "note": "Test"}')
echo "$INIT"

REFERENCE=$(echo "$INIT" | jq -r '.data.reference')
AUTH_URL=$(echo "$INIT"  | jq -r '.data.authorization_url')
echo "Open in browser: $AUTH_URL"

# 3. Pay with Paystack test card:
#    4084 0840 8408 4081  |  any future expiry  |  any CVV  |  PIN 0000  |  OTP 123456

# 4. Verify (only source of truth)
curl -s "$BASE_URL/payments/verify/$REFERENCE" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"

# 5. Confirm it shows up in history
curl -s "$BASE_URL/donations/contributions/my?paymentStatus=PAID&limit=5" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

## High-level flow

```
list -> pick donation -> bottom sheet (amount + note)
     -> POST /donations/:id/donate
     -> open authorization_url in WebView
     -> WebView navigates to callbackUrl host
     -> GET /payments/verify/:reference  <- SERVER decides
     -> success screen or failed screen
```

